      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aw",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1510896906,
      "version": 49,
      "versionNonce": 1972596346,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1781634444077,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "News-Feed design\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "News-Feed design\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "PHyGhlOw_OnDae8HoLTX8",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 548.0000000000001,
      "y": -123.5,
      "width": 1002.7393798828125,
      "height": 400,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "az",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1958552842,
      "version": 928,
      "versionNonce": 1920749094,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1781634444077,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Requirements\n* render initial feed quickly and load more posts as the user scrolls\n* support common feed interactions such as reaction/post creation\n* handle long lived sessions, stale data, common feed performance concerns\n* Do not need to go deep on feed ranking, ads delivery\nWhat kind of posts are supported\n* Primary text and image based posts (if time permit, we can discuss more type: video, carousel, etc...)\nPagination UX\n* infinite scrolling\n* For long lived session, it's worth to discuss how newer posts are surfaced at the top\nwithout disrupting what user is reading\nMobile device??\n* Whether application can stay web first or focus on mobile-specific interaction patterns\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Requirements\n* render initial feed quickly and load more posts as the user scrolls\n* support common feed interactions such as reaction/post creation\n* handle long lived sessions, stale data, common feed performance concerns\n* Do not need to go deep on feed ranking, ads delivery\nWhat kind of posts are supported\n* Primary text and image based posts (if time permit, we can discuss more type: video, carousel, etc...)\nPagination UX\n* infinite scrolling\n* For long lived session, it's worth to discuss how newer posts are surfaced at the top\nwithout disrupting what user is reading\nMobile device??\n* Whether application can stay web first or focus on mobile-specific interaction patterns\n\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "4JT8Wg2IDZNBDD-LCoiaK",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 447.2380425577501,
      "y": 215.4463645059201,
      "width": 287.59979248046875,
      "height": 50,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b00",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1044181770,
      "version": 41,
      "versionNonce": 1020497722,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1781634444077,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Architecture/high level design\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Architecture/high level design\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "4xuz2OHHb82EpL8ryzWsB",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 440.9487179365278,
      "y": 263.5572217462144,
      "width": 1241.039306640625,
      "height": 375,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b01",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 659662730,
      "version": 1544,
      "versionNonce": 1465620838,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1781634444077,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "** Rendering Approach **\n-- SSR: server generate the full HTML before sending it to browser, this leads to faster first paint and stronger SEO,\nonce HTML is loaded, the client hydrates the page to attech event listeners and enable interactivity\n-- CSR: server first deliver minimal HTML shell, and JS bundles. Browers then fetch data and renders the UI on client.\nCSR offer great interactivity once load because further update can happen without full page reloads. \nFirst load of CSR is typically slower than SSR and SEO is weaker\n-- Hybrid: combination of SSR and CSR. The initial pages is rendered on server for speed,\nwhile dynanamic update happen on client after hydration\n===> For personalized signed-in feed, the main benefit of SSR is performance, not SEO, since the content already personalized,\nsearch index will be less important than keeping the session interactive and responsive\n===> CSR is best default for home feed (signed-in). ==> long-session state mamagement tradeoff\n\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "** Rendering Approach **\n-- SSR: server generate the full HTML before sending it to browser, this leads to faster first paint and stronger SEO,\nonce HTML is loaded, the client hydrates the page to attech event listeners and enable interactivity\n-- CSR: server first deliver minimal HTML shell, and JS bundles. Browers then fetch data and renders the UI on client.\nCSR offer great interactivity once load because further update can happen without full page reloads. \nFirst load of CSR is typically slower than SSR and SEO is weaker\n-- Hybrid: combination of SSR and CSR. The initial pages is rendered on server for speed,\nwhile dynanamic update happen on client after hydration\n===> For personalized signed-in feed, the main benefit of SSR is performance, not SEO, since the content already personalized,\nsearch index will be less important than keeping the session interactive and responsive\n===> CSR is best default for home feed (signed-in). ==> long-session state mamagement tradeoff\n\n\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "u1-CopdW_i1ocYCi4oo23",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 421.00115921662007,
      "y": 539.6090503767571,
      "width": 1136.0191650390625,
      "height": 150,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b02",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 485129610,
      "version": 466,
      "versionNonce": 282171386,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1781634444077,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "==> To keep LCP competitive, CSR shell stil needs tight budget for app-shell bytes, initial feed data and critical JS.\nSSR or hybrid render can still be a good choice for public Feed page/marketing service (log out expereince)\nIn practice, NextJS or TanstackJS let products mix rendering strategy by route or surface when needed\n\n\n ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "==> To keep LCP competitive, CSR shell stil needs tight budget for app-shell bytes, initial feed data and critical JS.\nSSR or hybrid render can still be a good choice for public Feed page/marketing service (log out expereince)\nIn practice, NextJS or TanstackJS let products mix rendering strategy by route or surface when needed\n\n\n ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "Zce2ItT2CBoF0aRMLoKbB",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 395.64577176728307,
      "y": 649.9099380054831,
      "width": 1376.1990966796875,
      "height": 200,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b04",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1405034762,
      "version": 758,
      "versionNonce": 1353677990,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1781634444077,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "** Navigation approach (SPA vs MPA) **\n-- For Feed product, SPA is a strong default. The biggest reason is shared client state. Most user open a post from feed itself.\nIn SPA, the main post details such as text, media, etc... probably already in store, so navigation to post details page can feel nearly instant\nOnly need to fetch for comments/replies after navigation\n-- If using MPA (multi page), navigation tears down the current page state, and rebuilds from scratch.\nThat make transitions feel slower and discard useful in-memory statesuch as cached entities, optimistic updates, etc...\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "** Navigation approach (SPA vs MPA) **\n-- For Feed product, SPA is a strong default. The biggest reason is shared client state. Most user open a post from feed itself.\nIn SPA, the main post details such as text, media, etc... probably already in store, so navigation to post details page can feel nearly instant\nOnly need to fetch for comments/replies after navigation\n-- If using MPA (multi page), navigation tears down the current page state, and rebuilds from scratch.\nThat make transitions feel slower and discard useful in-memory statesuch as cached entities, optimistic updates, etc...\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
