    {
      "id": "RfxVU_FfPusSGxWElGyYf",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 369.3346050644851,
      "y": 823.6654195233077,
      "width": 249.95591735839844,
      "height": 35,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0k",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 369212362,
      "version": 36,
      "versionNonce": 402926970,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1781634444077,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "** Architecture **",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "** Architecture **",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "6Ot78jqRoGvAP8Xpvrd45",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1426.5007427543808,
      "y": 890.7505800292483,
      "width": 869.455322265625,
      "height": 240,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0l",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1213071766,
      "version": 1040,
      "versionNonce": 2075852582,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1781634444077,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "* View: this is what user interact with directly. Render data from store and trigger user action\n* Store: SOT for client-side state. It holds feed data, post, composer state, it keeps \ndifferent parts of inference consistent and lets the UI remain responsive even when the network is slow\n* Data access: abstract communication with API backend. Handle network request, response\nparsing, caching policy, navigation, retries, transformation, convert raw API response to \nstructure that easy to store to consume\n* Server: Expose HTTP endpoints for fetching the feed, fetching a single post, creating post, uploading media,\n\nIn SPA, Store and Data access layers are initialized once on first load, the persist \nand update throughout the session as user scroll, navigate and interact with posts\n\n ",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "* View: this is what user interact with directly. Render data from store and trigger user action\n* Store: SOT for client-side state. It holds feed data, post, composer state, it keeps \ndifferent parts of inference consistent and lets the UI remain responsive even when the network is slow\n* Data access: abstract communication with API backend. Handle network request, response\nparsing, caching policy, navigation, retries, transformation, convert raw API response to \nstructure that easy to store to consume\n* Server: Expose HTTP endpoints for fetching the feed, fetching a single post, creating post, uploading media,\n\nIn SPA, Store and Data access layers are initialized once on first load, the persist \nand update throughout the session as user scroll, navigate and interact with posts\n\n ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "RTwJjKLOq-gA8z_DZObQ1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 406.2484835893591,
      "y": 1623.6797484866393,
      "width": 190.76792907714844,
      "height": 170.02646756694418,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0o",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 105783766,
      "version": 299,
      "versionNonce": 1892970042,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1781634444077,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "** Data model **\n-- Post entities\n-- User entities\n-- Feed entities\n\n",
      "fontSize": 22.670195675592556,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "** Data model **\n-- Post entities\n-- User entities\n-- Feed entities\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "shh4mD-hk4gh24qa8-57P",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 713.7023653090121,
      "y": 1626.056816060015,
      "width": 1061.215087890625,
      "height": 600,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0p",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2066720150,
      "version": 431,
      "versionNonce": 127674982,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1781634444077,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "** Normalization **\nEntities should live in a normalized client store where each unique entity is stored exactly once and relationship are represented by IDs\nrather than nested copies.\n-- Main feed can be stored as one ordered list of post IDs while post detail views, comments and other feed-like surface can reference\nthe same canonical post, user, media records\n\ntype Media = {\n  id: string;\n  src: string;\n  previewSrc?: string;\n  alt: string;\n  width: number;\n  height: number;\n};\n\ntype ComposerDraft = {\n  body: PostBody;\n  mediaIds: string[];\n  uploadState: 'idle' | 'uploading' | 'failed';\n  submitState: 'idle' | 'submitting' | 'submitted' | 'failed';\n};\n\ntype Store = {\n  feedsById: Record<string, Feed>;\n  postsById: Record<string, Post>;\n  usersById: Record<string, User>;\n  mediaById: Record<string, Media>;\n  composerDraft: ComposerDraft;\n};\n",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "** Normalization **\nEntities should live in a normalized client store where each unique entity is stored exactly once and relationship are represented by IDs\nrather than nested copies.\n-- Main feed can be stored as one ordered list of post IDs while post detail views, comments and other feed-like surface can reference\nthe same canonical post, user, media records\n\ntype Media = {\n  id: string;\n  src: string;\n  previewSrc?: string;\n  alt: string;\n  width: number;\n  height: number;\n};\n\ntype ComposerDraft = {\n  body: PostBody;\n  mediaIds: string[];\n  uploadState: 'idle' | 'uploading' | 'failed';\n  submitState: 'idle' | 'submitting' | 'submitted' | 'failed';\n};\n\ntype Store = {\n  feedsById: Record<string, Feed>;\n  postsById: Record<string, Post>;\n  usersById: Record<string, User>;\n  mediaById: Record<string, Media>;\n  composerDraft: ComposerDraft;\n};\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "zQ3NVVYhofAo9SdPxuxHw",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 399.60755105624185,
      "y": 2210.6406517469622,
      "width": 1269.899169921875,
      "height": 725,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0s",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 508684310,
      "version": 2239,
      "versionNonce": 1868470010,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1781634444077,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "==> Data fetched from server does not need to arrive normalized. API simplicity favors the nested-then-client-normalized shape; \nserving weak client devices favors pushing normalization to server\nLarge production feed products typically do the latter\n\nAPI\n** HTTP API Get /feed -- with parameter such as count, cursor, direction (older, newer)\n** Support pagination \n---- offset base: ?offset=20&limit=10 to get the next 20 posts after the first 20\n====> Offset-based pagination is straightforward and easy to implement, \nbut it becomes inefficient and unreliable as the dataset grows or changes frequently. \nWhen new posts are inserted into the feed, offsets can shift, leading to duplicate or missing items.\n\n---- cursor base pagination: unique identifier such as postID or timestamp as cursor that marks the boundary between pages.\neg: \"the next 10 results after postIDX\". this is more stable and efficient because it does not depend on dataset's size\nor ordering at query time. Will work well in the environment where data is frequently updated. \n(where new post appear constantly and older post can be deleted, re-ranked, or refreshed)\n====> for new feed, cursor based pagination is a clear choice. It fits dynamic ordered feeds, where new posts\ncan be inserted, old post can disapper and ranking can change between requests. it enables bidirectional navigation, \nwhere user scroll down to fetch new post while client can separately checks for newer posts at the top.\n====> By combining cursor-based pagination with techniques like infinite scrolling and background fetching,\nfeed can remian continous and responsive even when large volumes of content are loaded behind the scene\n\n\n\n\n* Checking window.innerHeight before requesting data and size the initial page to determine # of feed being fetch\n* Subsequent fetched can then adapt based on the measured viewport height\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "==> Data fetched from server does not need to arrive normalized. API simplicity favors the nested-then-client-normalized shape; \nserving weak client devices favors pushing normalization to server\nLarge production feed products typically do the latter\n\nAPI\n** HTTP API Get /feed -- with parameter such as count, cursor, direction (older, newer)\n** Support pagination \n---- offset base: ?offset=20&limit=10 to get the next 20 posts after the first 20\n====> Offset-based pagination is straightforward and easy to implement, \nbut it becomes inefficient and unreliable as the dataset grows or changes frequently. \nWhen new posts are inserted into the feed, offsets can shift, leading to duplicate or missing items.\n\n---- cursor base pagination: unique identifier such as postID or timestamp as cursor that marks the boundary between pages.\neg: \"the next 10 results after postIDX\". this is more stable and efficient because it does not depend on dataset's size\nor ordering at query time. Will work well in the environment where data is frequently updated. \n(where new post appear constantly and older post can be deleted, re-ranked, or refreshed)\n====> for new feed, cursor based pagination is a clear choice. It fits dynamic ordered feeds, where new posts\ncan be inserted, old post can disapper and ranking can change between requests. it enables bidirectional navigation, \nwhere user scroll down to fetch new post while client can separately checks for newer posts at the top.\n====> By combining cursor-based pagination with techniques like infinite scrolling and background fetching,\nfeed can remian continous and responsive even when large volumes of content are loaded behind the scene\n\n\n\n\n* Checking window.innerHeight before requesting data and size the initial page to determine # of feed being fetch\n* Subsequent fetched can then adapt based on the measured viewport height\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "wRM656DU2KlbV-ACu2gTF",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 380.5910104692392,
      "y": 2789.904638729512,
      "width": 490.5397033691406,
      "height": 50,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
