    {
      "id": "oc5ahF_7aQb-Cv8slMBvr",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 225.75,
      "y": 358.5,
      "width": 1496.97900390625,
      "height": 300,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1d",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1048870822,
      "version": 1680,
      "versionNonce": 1032615674,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1781640475905,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "*** Rendering approach\n1) Input/textarea is not an option since these elements can only render plain text and not support formatted text\n2)  DOM with fake cursor will involves ton of complex text measuerment\n3) Preferrable: `contenteditable=\"true\"`, this support editing behavior, keyboard shortcut and rich text formatting\nWhat is the catch??\n--- Line formatting: only inline formatting supprorted. No built-in way to add element as heading/blockquoates\n--- Browser inconsitency supporting `contenteditable` leads to inconsistent behavior across platform\n--- Unsafe format: since content is HTML, it could introduce XSS attack ==> need sanitization, and store structed model (tree of nodes, JSON) instead.\n4) `<canvas />` element, render everything within it, it would require reimplement everything within canvas context. \n---- Google implementation, announce will move torward canvas base approach in 2021\n---- Provide full control with cost in maintenance, accessibility (re-implementing), incompatible with extensions. (that relies on DOM)\n---- Using canvas has much more performant approach with implementation cost. ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "*** Rendering approach\n1) Input/textarea is not an option since these elements can only render plain text and not support formatted text\n2)  DOM with fake cursor will involves ton of complex text measuerment\n3) Preferrable: `contenteditable=\"true\"`, this support editing behavior, keyboard shortcut and rich text formatting\nWhat is the catch??\n--- Line formatting: only inline formatting supprorted. No built-in way to add element as heading/blockquoates\n--- Browser inconsitency supporting `contenteditable` leads to inconsistent behavior across platform\n--- Unsafe format: since content is HTML, it could introduce XSS attack ==> need sanitization, and store structed model (tree of nodes, JSON) instead.\n4) `<canvas />` element, render everything within it, it would require reimplement everything within canvas context. \n---- Google implementation, announce will move torward canvas base approach in 2021\n---- Provide full control with cost in maintenance, accessibility (re-implementing), incompatible with extensions. (that relies on DOM)\n---- Using canvas has much more performant approach with implementation cost. ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
