    {
      "id": "Qo3vCyi64dcvKaTdXMs63",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 135.81358764261108,
      "y": 2623.13265874272,
      "width": 566.2596435546875,
      "height": 600,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#fff9db",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b24",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1687529850,
      "version": 42,
      "versionNonce": 719038522,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1781644943479,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "-- Map structure\n```\ntype NodeKey = string;\n\ntype NodeMap = Record<NodeKey, EditorNode>;\n\ninterface EditorNode {\n  parent: NodeKey | null;\n  prev: NodeKey | null;\n  next: NodeKey | null;\n  // Can contain other fields, depending on the node type.\n}\n\ninterface ElementNode extends EditorNode {\n  firstChild: NodeKey | null;\n  lastChild: NodeKey | null;\n  // Can contain other fields, depending on the node type.\n}\n\ninterface TextNode extends EditorNode {\n  text: string;\n}\n```\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "-- Map structure\n```\ntype NodeKey = string;\n\ntype NodeMap = Record<NodeKey, EditorNode>;\n\ninterface EditorNode {\n  parent: NodeKey | null;\n  prev: NodeKey | null;\n  next: NodeKey | null;\n  // Can contain other fields, depending on the node type.\n}\n\ninterface ElementNode extends EditorNode {\n  firstChild: NodeKey | null;\n  lastChild: NodeKey | null;\n  // Can contain other fields, depending on the node type.\n}\n\ninterface TextNode extends EditorNode {\n  text: string;\n}\n```\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "WH8CeH2FKbgIos09z30kZ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 823.747996681612,
      "y": 2977.8828838393497,
      "width": 1248.09912109375,
      "height": 350,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#fff9db",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b25",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1824154150,
      "version": 131,
      "versionNonce": 826149498,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1781644994148,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Advantages\n\n* Single-layer Map, extremely easy to clone both shallowly and deeply\n* O(1) access to any EditorNode if you know the NodeKey\n* Efficient removal and addition of child nodes because children are in a doubly linked list\n* Provides access to the parent node (not specific to the linked list implementation)\n* Reparenting of nodes is a matter of updating pointers\n\nDisadvantages\n* Updates made to the content require careful updating of pointers on multiple EditorNodes, similar to linked list manipulation\n* Knowing the size of the children requires counting. \nThis can be mitigated by maintaining a cached size field on ElementNodes that is updated whenever children are added/removed\n* Getting all the children of a node requires traversal from the first node to the last node\n* Hard for human eyes to read (not very important)",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Advantages\n\n* Single-layer Map, extremely easy to clone both shallowly and deeply\n* O(1) access to any EditorNode if you know the NodeKey\n* Efficient removal and addition of child nodes because children are in a doubly linked list\n* Provides access to the parent node (not specific to the linked list implementation)\n* Reparenting of nodes is a matter of updating pointers\n\nDisadvantages\n* Updates made to the content require careful updating of pointers on multiple EditorNodes, similar to linked list manipulation\n* Knowing the size of the children requires counting. \nThis can be mitigated by maintaining a cached size field on ElementNodes that is updated whenever children are added/removed\n* Getting all the children of a node requires traversal from the first node to the last node\n* Hard for human eyes to read (not very important)",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
