    {
      "id": "cP_tll3UtKOZYnz4twzav",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 125.55559879983048,
      "y": -238.92304926620477,
      "width": 1884.3388671875,
      "height": 350,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#fff9db",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2J",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1044457466,
      "version": 194,
      "versionNonce": 242706746,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1781650965769,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Use an immutable editor state as the source of truth: Model the document as an EditorState with a node map, text nodes, element nodes,\n and explicit selection state, so edits are predictable, efficient, and independent of the DOM.\n\n2. Represent structure for fast editing: Store parent/child/sibling relationships with pointers like parent, prev, next, firstChild, and lastChild,\n allowing O(1) traversal and localized structural updates.\n\n3. Render through controlled DOM reconciliation: Each node owns createDOM and updateDOM, \nwhile the contenteditable DOM is treated only as rendered output, not the source of truth.\n\n4. Route all mutations through commands and plugins: \nUser actions, toolbar actions, paste, keyboard input, and programmatic edits all become commands, allowing plugins, transforms, and listeners to compose cleanly.\n\n5. Commit changes through a single update loop: \neditor.update() creates a pending state, clones only dirty nodes, runs transforms, diffs against the active state, and patches only the changed DOM subtrees for performance and consistency.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Use an immutable editor state as the source of truth: Model the document as an EditorState with a node map, text nodes, element nodes,\n and explicit selection state, so edits are predictable, efficient, and independent of the DOM.\n\n2. Represent structure for fast editing: Store parent/child/sibling relationships with pointers like parent, prev, next, firstChild, and lastChild,\n allowing O(1) traversal and localized structural updates.\n\n3. Render through controlled DOM reconciliation: Each node owns createDOM and updateDOM, \nwhile the contenteditable DOM is treated only as rendered output, not the source of truth.\n\n4. Route all mutations through commands and plugins: \nUser actions, toolbar actions, paste, keyboard input, and programmatic edits all become commands, allowing plugins, transforms, and listeners to compose cleanly.\n\n5. Commit changes through a single update loop: \neditor.update() creates a pending state, clones only dirty nodes, runs transforms, diffs against the active state, and patches only the changed DOM subtrees for performance and consistency.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
